.TH AM_GET_CONSTRUCTORS 3 "August 2026" "Audit Multiplexer" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
am_get_constructors, am_get_destructors \- retrieve shared object initialization and finalization functions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fB#include <audit_multiplexer.h>\fR

\fBstd::vector<am_init_fini_fn_t> am_get_constructors(struct link_map *\fImap\fB);\fR
\fBstd::vector<am_init_fini_fn_t> am_get_destructors(struct link_map *\fImap\fB);\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR am_get_constructors ()
and
.BR am_get_destructors ()
functions inspect the dynamic section of a loaded shared object (represented by its \fIlink_map\fR) to locate its initialization (constructor) and finalization (destructor) functions. 
.PP
These utility functions are primarily intended for use within the
.BR la_objopen (3)
hook of an audit library. Because the dynamic linker loads objects sequentially, an auditor may need to manually execute an object's constructors in its own context or a sandbox environment before the library is fully exposed to the host application.
.PP
The functions inspect the \fBDT_INIT\fR and \fBDT_INIT_ARRAY\fR (or \fBDT_FINI\fR and \fBDT_FINI_ARRAY\fR) tags within the ELF dynamic section and adjust the parsed addresses using the load bias (\fIl_addr\fR) of the \fIlink_map\fR.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Both functions return a \fBstd::vector\fR of function pointers of type \fBam_init_fini_fn_t\fR. If the object has no constructors or destructors, or if the \fImap\fR pointer is invalid, an empty vector is returned.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rtld-audit (7),
.BR dlinfo (3)